$$
\text{Moles of } O_{2} (n_{O_{2}}) = \frac{\text{Volume of } O_{2}}{22.7}
$$

$$
n_{O_{2}} = \frac{2.8375 \text{ litres}}{22.7 \text{ litres/mol}} = 0.125 \text{ moles}
$$

$$
\text{Molecules of } O_{2} = \text{moles} \times N_{A}
$$

$$
= 0.125 \times 6.022 \times 10^{23}
$$

$$
= 7.527 \times 10^{22} \text{ molecules}
$$

Thus, the number of molecules is \(7.527\times 10^{22}\) and the number of moles is \(0.125\) mol.

